---
source: crates/chain-syntax/tests/it/bad.rs
expression: "annotate(&text, &parsed.diagnostics)"
---
  1 | chain 1
  2 | eq #1 hp=90kHZ lp=
    |          ^ 2:10: error E107: `kHZ` is not a unit; did you mean `kHz`?
    |                   ^ 2:19: error E106: a value is missing at the end of the line
  3 | compressor #2 ratio 4 "Glue
    |               ^ 3:15: error E106: `ratio` needs `=` and a value, such as `ratio=1`
    |                     ^ 3:21: error E106: expected `key=value`, found a number
    |                       ^ 3:23: error E108: this quoted text has no closing `"`
  4 | delay #3 time=1/0 feedback=30%
    |               ^ 4:15: error E106: a note value is a count and a division, such as `1/4`, `1/8.` or `1/8t`
  5 | saturation #4 drive=-dB % curve=tube
    |                     ^ 5:21: error E106: a number must have a digit after its sign
    |                         ^ 5:25: error E106: `%` cannot start a token here
  6 | lfo #5 -> #4.drive
    |        ^ 6:8: error E109: `->` links go on a modulator, in a `mods` block
